---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="What Primitive Bytes is about, and what I'm building."
	pubDate={new Date('November 13 2026')}
>
	<p>
		Primitive Bytes is about the small, versioned configs that make AI agents safer and easier
		to build with: lockfiles for tools, contracts for servers, manifests for agents. Each one is
		owned by someone, reviewed like code, and enforced by a tool rather than read by a person.
	</p>
	<p>
		I'm building these in the open. The first is <code>reef lock</code>, which pins every MCP
		tool's description and schemas so a server can't quietly change what your agent reads. It
		lives in <a href="https://github.com/FatherBrian/trellis/tree/main/reef">Reef</a>, an
		open-source MCP gateway.
	</p>
	<p>
		Find me on <a href="https://github.com/FatherBrian">GitHub</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>
